      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Build a general serial algorithmic candidate. Replace per-column quadratic bubble sort and quadratic mode counting with a reference-compatible O(rows log rows) stable sort (reuse scratch storage) plus linear equal-run mode detection. Preserve source ordering: mean/harmonic before sorting, variance over sorted values using the original mean, exact equality/tie behavior, and output formatting. Handle signed zero, NaN/token edge cases only if they match the reference.\",\"B\":\"Build a coarse-grained 4-core candidate: parallelize independent whole-column work, retain deterministic per-column arithmetic, and use a dimension/work-based serial fallback so thread startup cannot lose on the 9.315 ms baseline. Measure complete process time at 1/2/4 workers; do not assume parallel reductions or combining changes is safe.\",\"C\":\"Build a distinct low-level serial candidate. Investigate buffered standards-compatible input parsing, fused independent scans, removal of repeated allocations, and safe numeric-kernel improvements; retain arithmetic order where rounding can affect %.1f output. Compare library/custom stable sorting approaches, but accept only variants preserving the source-observed mode and comparison semantics on broad inputs.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only validated candidates. Differential-check broad valid matrices (small/large, odd/even rows, duplicates/ties, zero/negative/extreme doubles and input formatting), then measure baseline, each candidate, and only compatible combinations repeatedly under the unchanged environment. The measured baseline is already very short and integration may regress; retain the fastest correct end-to-end program, including baseline if necessary.\",\"analysis\":\"The valid baseline averages 9.315 ms on a 4-core ARM64 target, so fixed I/O and thread costs matter. The clear general bottlenecks in the source are quadratic sorting and mode calculation; parsing and pow/scans are secondary. Preserve exact observable behavior rather than exploiting one-decimal output or test-specific values, especially the source's sorted-mode/tie and floating-point evaluation behavior.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"80165ea50f9f18b39c609b86778a8034f4f91c9c7496d719117dc17a7861586f\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Build a general serial algorithmic candidate. Replace per-column quadratic bubble sort and quadratic mode counting with a reference-compatible O(rows log rows) stable sort (reuse scratch storage) plus linear equal-run mode detection. Preserve source ordering: mean/harmonic before sorting, variance over sorted values using the original mean, exact equality/tie behavior, and output formatting. Handle signed zero, NaN/token edge cases only if they match the reference.\",\"B\":\"Build a coarse-grained 4-core candidate: parallelize independent whole-column work, retain deterministic per-column arithmetic, and use a dimension/work-based serial fallback so thread startup cannot lose on the 9.315 ms baseline. Measure complete process time at 1/2/4 workers; do not assume parallel reductions or combining changes is safe.\",\"C\":\"Build a distinct low-level serial candidate. Investigate buffered standards-compatible input parsing, fused independent scans, removal of repeated allocations, and safe numeric-kernel improvements; retain arithmetic order where rounding can affect %.1f output. Compare library/custom stable sorting approaches, but accept only variants preserving the source-observed mode and comparison semantics on broad inputs.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only validated candidates. Differential-check broad valid matrices (small/large, odd/even rows, duplicates/ties, zero/negative/extreme doubles and input formatting), then measure baseline, each candidate, and only compatible combinations repeatedly under the unchanged environment. The measured baseline is already very short and integration may regress; retain the fastest correct end-to-end program, including baseline if necessary.\",\"analysis\":\"The valid baseline averages 9.315 ms on a 4-core ARM64 target, so fixed I/O and thread costs matter. The clear general bottlenecks in the source are quadratic sorting and mode calculation; parsing and pow/scans are secondary. Preserve exact observable behavior rather than exploiting one-decimal output or test-specific values, especially the source's sorted-mode/tie and floating-point evaluation behavior.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"nonce\":\"b0c8df830a4341fe88834a963a6d0694\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"80165ea50f9f18b39c609b86778a8034f4f91c9c7496d719117dc17a7861586f\",\"session_id\":\"16cc609c0eae4b378c00819505095c0f\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"59f406f76c66ae01f089ed32c517f160ce9bd08ad5020c4fa9c06e6ccb9808a0\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":12111,\"output_tokens\":7657,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":7250}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":19768,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
